From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GapKeep <noreply@gapkeep.org>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 12:50:25 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] Build the QR code reader without exceptions (ZX_THROW) or
 thread_local

For bare-metal targets without an exception runtime or TLS (GapKeep, on
Circle on a Raspberry Pi Zero):

- ZX_THROW(e) in ZXConfig.h: `throw e` when exceptions are enabled, and
  otherwise a call to ZXing::Fatal("e"), which the application provides
  and which must not return. Used for the throws in the files the QR code
  reader is built from; the QR payload decoder itself does not throw on
  any input (see the previous change). librscpp keeps a plain throw unless
  ZXConfig.h was included first.
- ZX_THREAD_LOCAL can be set by the build (e.g. -DZX_THREAD_LOCAL=static
  for a single-threaded program); the default is still thread_local.
